WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.165 --> 00:00:04.610
Agarfa and the Drops of the Garoé

2
00:00:05.245 --> 00:00:11.050
When the Bimbapes lived on El Hierro,
Agarfa walked to the Garoé every morning.

3
00:00:11.765 --> 00:00:18.005
The mist became tangled in its branches
and turned into drops that fell into stone

4
00:00:18.005 --> 00:00:19.005
basins.

5
00:00:19.445 --> 00:00:22.090
The whole community depended on that
water.

6
00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:29.590
Agarfa filled the jars slowly so as not to
waste any, repeating: “Branch by branch,

7
00:00:29.685 --> 00:00:32.930
drop by drop, the Garoé gives us its
water.”

8
00:00:34.305 --> 00:00:38.230
One day, unfamiliar sails appeared on the
horizon.

9
00:00:38.985 --> 00:00:44.485
The older people feared that the newcomers
would find the tree and take control of

10
00:00:44.485 --> 00:00:45.485
the water source.

11
00:00:46.305 --> 00:00:52.265
They covered the path with branches and
asked Agarfa to carry the jars along

12
00:00:52.265 --> 00:00:58.225
another route. The girl made her way
through the mist without revealing where

13
00:00:58.225 --> 00:00:59.225
the Garoé stood.

14
00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:02.590
For many days, they kept the secret.

15
00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:06.945
Traditional stories give different
accounts of how the tree was later

16
00:01:06.945 --> 00:01:12.585
discovered. They also tell of a great
storm that brought it down many years

17
00:01:12.585 --> 00:01:13.585
later.

18
00:01:13.925 --> 00:01:16.490
But the story of the Garoé did not
disappear.

19
00:01:17.185 --> 00:01:22.805
Families kept telling how a tree could
comb the mist and turn it into water for a

20
00:01:22.805 --> 00:01:23.805
whole island.

21
00:01:24.365 --> 00:01:30.265
When they remembered it, everyone would
say: “Branch by branch, drop by drop, the

22
00:01:30.265 --> 00:01:32.170
Garoé gives us its water.”

